": \"075442b68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 25436, \"chunk_count\": 14, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:51\", \"token_count\": 7169, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"- `SRC-ISSUE-06` — [opentelemetry-go-contrib-8078.md](../opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8078.md)\\n\\n- `SRC-PR-02` — [community-3000.md](../opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md)\\n\\n- `SRC-PR-07` — [opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md](../opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md)\\n\\n- `SRC-NOTE-04` — [entry-3479584781.md](../opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md)\\n\\n- `SRC-NOTE-05` — [entry-3479626706.md](../opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479626706.md)\\n\\n- `SRC-NOTE-06` — [entry-3479655348.md](../opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md)\\n\\n- `SRC-MILE-02` — [milestone-13145551.md](../opentelemetry/milestones/milestone-13145551.md)\\n\\n- `SRC-MILE-04` — [milestone-14282228.md](../opentelemetry/milestones/milestone-14282228.md)\\n\\n# WS-05: Contrib Modules\\n\\n**Status**: in_progress\\n\\n**Priority**: P0\\n\\n**Owner**: Damien Mathieu (contrib SIG context)\\n\\n**Project**: opentelemetry-go-contrib / community\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-03-08\\n\\n## Next Update Needed\\n\\n- Publication of the completed `#6609` work and GitHub issue update; any release containing `#7254`; whether `#8106` merged; otelgrpc stabilization progress; Explorer implementation beyond the proposal PR.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"src issu 06 opentelemetri go contrib 8078 md opentelemetri issu opentelemetri go contrib 8078 md src pr 02 communiti 3000 md opentelemetri pull communiti 3000 md src pr 07 opentelemetri go contrib 8014 md opentelemetri pull opentelemetri go contrib 8014 md src note 04 entri 3479584781 md opentelemetri meet note entri 3479584781 md src note 05 entri 3479626706 md opentelemetri meet note entri 3479626706 md src note 06 entri 3479655348 md opentelemetri meet note entri 3479655348 md src mile 02 mileston 13145551 md opentelemetri mileston mileston 13145551 md src mile 04 mileston 14282228 md opentelemetri mileston mileston 14282228 md w 05 contrib modul status in _ progress prioriti p0 owner damien mathieu contrib sig context project opentelemetri go contrib communiti last updat 2026 03 08 next updat need public of the complet 6609 work and github issu updat ani releas contain 7254 whether 8106 merg otelgrpc stabil progress explor implement beyond the propos pr\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"6e42a59a8da711f18c2f6b4f6cd8a654\", \"document_keyword\": \"work-states/WS-05-contrib.md\", \"id\": \"0df5ebf381bf4c17\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.35557111179469064, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20731707399241522, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7014972, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"work-states/WS-05-contrib.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"6e42a59a8da711f18c2f6b4f6cd8a654\", \"name\": \"work-states/WS-05-contrib.md\", \"location\": \"work-states/WS-05-contrib.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 6662, \"chunk_count\": 12, \"create_date\": \"2026-08-01T20:49:27\", \"update_date\": \"2026-08-01T20:49:47\", \"token_count\": 6248, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"work-state\"}}}, {\"content\": \"To summarise I feel it is beneficial to be using weaver to document/describe the signals as well as the instrumentation emitting them as they should be sharing significant amounts of data. This way the eco-system Explorer can then focus on presenting and making discoverable the emitted definitions.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**jack-berg** — 2025-11-10T15:29:30Z\\n\\nWhen I read this proposal, I see this project as a an attempt to build a new registry (registry 2.0). I'm very supportive of this as I've been complaining about various deficiencies of the registry for some time.\\n\\nSignificantly, the proposal is to launch the new effort in parallel to the existing registry, allowing the contributors to iterate quickly and avoid the friction of a bunch of up front data model design work and consensus gathering.\\n\\nLater, once we've worked out the sharp edges, we can merge registry 1.0 into registry 2.0, and EOL registry 1.0.\\n\\nSome thoughts:\\n\\n- The registry already has a data model for capturing meta data about components (schema [here](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry.io)), but its insufficient. As you note, there's all sorts of data which is important to capture and visualize for end users, which as of now, is very difficult for users to discover. The key examples being: configuration schema, schema of telemetry emitted, instructions on how to get started.\\n\\n- The [registry](https://opentelemetry.io/ecosystem/registry/) already has tools for searching for components, and displaying bits of information about them, but its insufficient. More than anything else, the registry is an index of links, requiring the user to follow the link and find installation / configuration / telemetry schema details in the linked website / repository. Except this information is no always available, and when it is, there's no standardization about the display. A richer registry schema would allow a richer / more useful visualization experience.\\n\\n- The registry already has [tooling](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry.io/blob/main/scripts/registry-scanner/index.mjs) for scanning for project repositories and creating / updating registry component entries. The problem is, its all centralized in the `opentelemetry.io` project and standardized, meaning that its only possible to scrape the types of meta data which can scraped from a central script. In his prototype, @jaydeluca has built tooling which leverages domain knowledge specific to the `opentelemetry-java-instrumentation` project, and is therefore able to generate much richer meta data that is captured by the registry today. Any effort for a better registry is probably going to require some coordination between the repos where components live (i.e SDK, instrumentation, contrib, collector, etc) and the `opentelemetry.io` repo. Some shared tooling can / should be centralized in `opentelemetry.io`, but the repos should also work to do a better job of publishing the types of meta data that can't be generated through simple scanner scripts.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"to summaris i feel it is benefici to be use weaver to document describ the signal a well a the instrument emit them a they should be share signific amount of data this way the eco system explor can then focus on present and make discover the emit definit jack berg 2025 11 10t15 29 30z when i read this propos i see this project a a an attempt to build a new registri registri 20 i m veri support of this a i ve been complain about various defici of the registri for some time signific the propos is to launch the new effort in parallel to the exist registri allow the contributor to iter quick and avoid the friction of a bunch of up front data model design work and consensus gather later onc we ve work out the sharp edg we can merg registri 10 into registri 20 and eol registri 10 some thought the registri alreadi ha a data model for captur meta data about compon schema here http github com open telemetri opentelemetri io but it insuffici a you note there s all sort of data which is import to captur and visual for end user which a of now is veri difficult for user to discov the key exampl be configur schema schema of telemetri emit instruct on how to get start the registri http opentelemetri io ecosystem registri alreadi ha tool for search for compon and display bit of inform about them but it insuffici more than anyth els the registri is an index of link requir the user to follow the link and find instal configur telemetri schema detail in the link websit repositori except this inform is no alway avail and when it is there s no standard about the display a richer registri schema would allow a richer more use visual experi the registri alreadi ha tool http github com open telemetri opentelemetri io blob main script registri scanner index mjs for scan for project repositori and creat updat registri compon entri the problem is it all central in the opentelemetri io project and standard mean that it onli possibl to scrape the type of meta data which can scrape from a central script in his prototyp jaydeluca ha built tool which leverag domain knowledg specif to the opentelemetri java instrument project and is therefor abl to generat much richer meta data that is captur by the registri today ani effort for a better registri is probabl go to requir some coordin between the repo where compon live i e sdk instrument contrib collector etc and the opentelemetri io repo some share tool can should be central in opentelemetri io but the repo should also work to do a better job of publish the type of meta data that can t be generat through simpl scanner script\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"075442b68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"id\": \"a93597843abdec73\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3533163314376858, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.19512195205383698, \"vector_similarity\": 0.72243655, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"075442b68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 25436, \"chunk_count\": 14, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:51\", \"token_count\": 7169, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"- `T002 / #7254` — Opened 2025-04-23 by `XSAM`; milestoned to `v1.39.0` on 2025-09-18; discussed 2025-10-30 as a possible otelhttp stabilization blocker with Robert assigned to draft clarification `(SRC-NOTE-06)`; moved to `v1.40.0` on 2025-12-04 `(SRC-MILE-04)`; closed 2026-01-13 `(SRC-ISSUE-02)`. No release Source after `v1.39.0` establishes delivery.\\n\\n- `T003 / #8059` — Closed 2025-12-04 `(SRC-ISSUE-05)`. Linked PR `#8106` appears only as a cross-reference; merge/release not established in Sources.\\n\\n- `T004 / #8078` — Closed as not planned 2025-10-31 `(SRC-ISSUE-06)`.\\n\\n- `T006 / community#3000` — Proposal opened 2025-09-19 by `jaydeluca`; 2025-10-30 meeting required semconv alignment, Weaver compatibility, and schema validation `(SRC-NOTE-06)`; merged/closed 2025-12-01 `(SRC-PR-02)`. Explorer product delivery not established.\\n\\n# WS-05: Contrib Modules\\n\\n**Status**: in_progress\\n\\n**Priority**: P0\\n\\n**Owner**: Damien Mathieu (contrib SIG context)\\n\\n**Project**: opentelemetry-go-contrib / community\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-03-08\\n\\n## Sources\\n\\n- `SRC-ISSUE-01` — [opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md](../opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md)\\n\\n- `SRC-PR-01` — [opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md](../opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md)\\n\\n- `SRC-ISSUE-02` — [opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md](../opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md)\\n\\n- `SRC-ISSUE-05` — [opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md](../opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md)\\n\\n- `SRC-ISSUE-06` — [opentelemetry-go-contrib-8078.md](../opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8078.md)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"t002 7254 open 2025 04 23 by xsam mileston to v1 39 0 on 2025 09 18 discuss 2025 10 30 a a possibl otelhttp stabil blocker with robert assign to draft clarif src note 06 move to v1 400 on 2025 12 04 src mile 04 close 2026 01 13 src issu 02 no releas sourc after v1 39 0 establish deliveri t003 8059 close 2025 12 04 src issu 05 link pr 8106 appear onli a a cross refer merg releas not establish in sourc t004 8078 close a not plan 2025 10 31 src issu 06 t006 communiti 3000 propos open 2025 09 19 by jaydeluca 2025 10 30 meet requir semconv align weaver compat and schema valid src note 06 merg close 2025 12 01 src pr 02 explor product deliveri not establish w 05 contrib modul status in _ progress prioriti p0 owner damien mathieu contrib sig context project opentelemetri go contrib communiti last updat 2026 03 08 sourc src issu 01 opentelemetri go contrib 5946 md opentelemetri issu opentelemetri go contrib 5946 md src pr 01 opentelemetri go contrib 6609 md opentelemetri pull opentelemetri go contrib 6609 md src issu 02 opentelemetri go contrib 7254 md opentelemetri issu opentelemetri go contrib 7254 md src issu 05 opentelemetri go contrib 8059 md opentelemetri issu opentelemetri go contrib 8059 md src issu 06 opentelemetri go contrib 8078 md opentelemetri issu opentelemetri go contrib 8078 md\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"6e42a59a8da711f18c2f6b4f6cd8a654\", \"document_keyword\": \"work-states/WS-05-contrib.md\", \"id\": \"8866947187739703\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.34771623443768584, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.19512195205383698, \"vector_similarity\": 0.70376956, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"work-states/WS-05-contrib.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"6e42a59a8da711f18c2f6b4f6cd8a654\", \"name\": \"work-states/WS-05-contrib.md\", \"location\": \"work-states/WS-05-contrib.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 6662, \"chunk_count\": 12, \"create_date\": \"2026-08-01T20:49:27\", \"update_date\": \"2026-08-01T20:49:47\", \"token_count\": 6248, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"work-state\"}}}, {\"content\": \"---\\n\\n**svrnm** — 2025-11-18T07:54:04Z\\n\\n> When I read this proposal, I see this project as a an attempt to build a new registry (registry 2.0). I'm very supportive of this as I've been complaining about various deficiencies of the registry for some time.\\n\\nIt absolutely is! That's why I am in favour of this project so much. The registry has been a building block of our project from day 1, but besides a few cosmetic changes we never lifted it to a proper solution.\\n\\n> Significantly, the proposal is to launch the new effort in parallel to the existing registry, allowing the contributors to iterate quickly and avoid the friction of a bunch of up front data model design work and consensus gathering.\\n\\nYes 🙌 \\n\\n> Later, once we've worked out the sharp edges, we can merge registry 1.0 into registry 2.0, and EOL registry 1.0.\\n\\nI can barely wait for it ;) \\n\\n>     * The registry already has a data model for capturing meta data about components (schema [here](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry.io?rgh-link-date=2025-11-10T15%3A29%3A30Z)), but its insufficient. As you note, there's all sorts of data which is important to capture and visualize for end users, which as of now, is very difficult for users to discover. The key examples being: configuration schema, schema of telemetry emitted, instructions on how to get started.\\n\\nYes, we can learn and take from the existing schema, but overall it's insufficient. \\n\\n>     * The [registry](https://opentelemetry.io/ecosystem/registry/) already has tools for searching for components, and displaying bits of information about them, but its insufficient. More than anything else, the registry is an index of links, requiring the user to follow the link and find installation / configuration / telemetry schema details in the linked website / repository. Except this information is no always available, and when it is, there's no standardization about the display. A richer registry schema would allow a richer / more useful visualization experience.\\n\\nThe registry as of today does what it was intended to do, provide a quick glance into all the things opentelemetry. but as the project evolved, the registry didn't, and as you lined out it's missing a lot of details and nuances, so this project aims to help with that. \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"svrnm 2025 11 18t07 54 04z when i read this propos i see this project a a an attempt to build a new registri registri 20 i m veri support of this a i ve been complain about various defici of the registri for some time it absolut is that s whi i am in favour of this project so much the registri ha been a build block of our project from day 1 but besid a few cosmet chang we never lift it to a proper solut signific the propos is to launch the new effort in parallel to the exist registri allow the contributor to iter quick and avoid the friction of a bunch of up front data model design work and consensus gather yes later onc we ve work out the sharp edg we can merg registri 10 into registri 20 and eol registri 10i can bare wait for it the registri alreadi ha a data model for captur meta data about compon schema here http github com open telemetri opentelemetri io rgh link date 2025 11 10t15 3a29 3a30z but it insuffici a you note there s all sort of data which is import to captur and visual for end user which a of now is veri difficult for user to discov the key exampl be configur schema schema of telemetri emit instruct on how to get start yes we can learn and take from the exist schema but overal it s insuffici the registri http opentelemetri io ecosystem registri alreadi ha tool for search for compon and display bit of inform about them but it insuffici more than anyth els the registri is an index of link requir the user to follow the link and find instal configur telemetri schema detail in the link websit repositori except this inform is no alway avail and when it is there s no standard about the display a richer registri schema would allow a richer more use visual experi the registri a of today doe what it wa intend to do provid a quick glanc into all the thing opentelemetri but a the project evolv the registri didn t and a you line out it s miss a lot of detail and nuanc so this project aim to help with that\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"075442b68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"id\": \"7a9047e037861203\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33018641572367635, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1707317081766805, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7022474, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"075442b68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 25436, \"chunk_count\": 14, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:51\", \"token_count\": 7169, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"The initial POC focused on a static-site approach which is much simpler to operate, has _almost_ no ongoing maintenance burden, and still meets our immediate needs. Personally, I'd much prefer a solution that requires as little operational overhead as possible.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**trask** — 2025-10-01T19:11:49Z\\n\\n+1 on optimizing for low operational overhead since that's an area where we struggle as an Open Source project\\n\\n---\\n\\n**thompson-tomo** — 2025-10-06T05:26:18Z\\n\\nI am all for a lower operational overhead but I do get worried when I see suggestions to build something as that can create tech debt especially when it is not a key part of the organisation business/objective. Hence suggestion to use an established product.\\n\\nWith the objective of low operational effort and static site generation in mind, we should be exploring how weaver can be contribute to the solution.\\n\\nWhat I could foresee is:\\n\\n- User defines a weaver registry file which imports signals from the sem conv registry\\n\\n- User refines the imported signals based on what they are implementing\\n\\n- User defines either a seperate implementation metadata file or adds it to the registry file. TBD\\n\\n- Weaver codegen runs ie `weaver implementation generate` for the refined signals and metadata. This would produce boilerplate code which is used in the implementation and exports a yaml definition file (resolved schema).\\n\\n- the exported yaml could be added to the eco-system which is proceeded by `weaver implementation describe` to emit the static content.\\n\\nAll of that would be reusable especially if the repo/package readme could also be generated in the same manner.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**jaydeluca** — 2025-10-06T10:17:57Z\\n\\n@thompson-tomo who is a \\\"user\\\" in your example? This project is specifically aimed at creating documentation for java instrumentation (and possibly the collector and other languages as a stretch goal). There are over 250 instrumentations in the java project, and at this time none of them use weaver to define their attributes. I have experimented with introducing weaver to the project in order to generate metrics/attributes for an instrumentation, but as of this time, there are no existing plans by the SIG to rewrite everything in that repo to use weaver (that I am aware of).\\n\\nI am all for integrating weaver where it makes sense, but if we are saying we need to convert that repo to use weaver before we move ahead with this project, I fear it would be a very long time before we could deliver anything useful. There's also a significant number of things involved here that go beyond just documenting the attributes that I don't think weaver helps with.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"the initi poc focus on a static site approach which is much simpler to oper ha _ almost _ no ongo mainten burden and still meet our immedi need person i d much prefer a solut that requir a littl oper overhead a possibl trask 2025 10 01t19 11 49z 1 on optim for low oper overhead sinc that s an area where we struggl a an open sourc project thompson tomo 2025 10 06t05 26 18z i am all for a lower oper overhead but i do get worri when i see suggest to build someth a that can creat tech debt especi when it is not a key part of the organis busi object henc suggest to use an establish product with the object of low oper effort and static site generat in mind we should be explor how weaver can be contribut to the solut what i could forese is user defin a weaver registri file which import signal from the sem conv registri user refin the import signal base on what they are implement user defin either a seper implement metadata file or add it to the registri file tbd weaver codegen run ie weaver implement generat for the refin signal and metadata this would produc boilerpl code which is use in the implement and export a yaml definit file resolv schema the export yaml could be ad to the eco system which is proceed by weaver implement describ to emit the static content all of that would be reusabl especi if the repo packag readm could also be generat in the same manner jaydeluca 2025 10 06t10 17 57z thompson tomo who is a user in your exampl this project is speci